{{also|zoöphyte}}
==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|zoöphyte|zoophite|zoöphite}}

===Etymology===
From {{confix|en|zoo|phyte}}, after {{uder|en|frm|zoophyte}}; later reinforced by scientific Latin {{taxfmt|Zoophyta|order}}.

===Pronunciation===
*{{IPA|en|/ˈzəʊəfaɪt/|/ˈzuːfaɪt/|a=UK}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|biology|historical}} An animal thought to have the characteristics of a [[plant]], later specifically an invertebrate of the (former) group Zoophyta, comprising [[sponge]]s, [[coral]]s and [[sea anemone]]s. {{defdate|from 17th c.}}
# {{lb|en|biology|historical}} A [[plant]] believed to have the characteristics of an [[animal]], especially a [[sensitive plant]] or [[vegetable lamb]]. {{defdate|from 17th c.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1665|author=w:Robert Hooke|title=Micrographia|section=XIX
|passage=And besides, as there are many '''''Zoophyts''''', and sensitive Plants {{...}} so have we, in some Authors, Instances of Plants turning into Animals, and Animals into Plants, and the like {{...}}}}

